WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.959 --> 00:00:04.850
Hey youtubers it's Charlie and Teen Wolf is
back for the Summer.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:08.769
Since a lot of you asked me to do videos for
it I'm going to be doing weekly vids.

00:00:08.769 --> 00:00:11.460
I'm not planning on doing Q&amp;A videos or anything
like that, but if you want me to do bonus

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.740
videos like I did for Game of Thrones let
me know.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:17.070
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:21.269
This episode is kind of that limbo state between
the old crew when we still had Allison and

00:00:21.269 --> 00:00:23.890
Isaac and the new Team with Malia and Kira.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:27.740
There's a bunch of new characters this season
and it's going to completely change the tone

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:32.630
of the show, but we had to have this episode
to bridge the gap, following up what happened

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:33.630
to Derek.

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:38.460
The theme of Season 4 overall is "Can't Go
Back", which is interesting because this week

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.019
we went on a Mexican Road Trip.

00:00:41.019 --> 00:00:43.969
So what I'm going to do is my top 5 moments
from the episode, then my review and then

00:00:43.969 --> 00:00:47.600
I'll talk about what's going to to be new
in Season 4 and why that's a good thing.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:51.809
I'll just tease right now, if you liked Season
1, you're going to love Season 4.

00:00:51.809 --> 00:00:55.219
So careful for spoilers from the episode in
case you haven't seen it, but here we go.

00:00:55.219 --> 00:00:57.929
Number 5 - Wolfsbane Gas Dance Party

00:00:57.929 --> 00:01:01.769
The reason they went to the club was because
they found werewolf hunter shell casings with

00:01:01.769 --> 00:01:05.920
the insignia of that family, the Calaveres,
they're another hunter family just like the

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:06.920
Argents.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:08.190
They're not really bad or good.

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:11.610
They're just nazi's about the Hunter's Code.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:18.000
The Dance Party is just the introduction to
the 'new team', like their grand stage entrance.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.840
I love that Malia was the one who had to tell
Kira to 'fit in', when she's the worst person

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:23.490
in the world at fitting in.

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:27.200
The two of them are still kind of outsiders
even after spending season 3 trying to help

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.570
Scott and Stiles.

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:33.049
There was a bit of Malia Kira 'ship teasing
here, but I don't think that's going anywhere.

00:01:33.049 --> 00:01:38.260
I think the show is really going to push the
Malia Stiles and Kira Scott ships.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:40.860
Number 4 - Teen Wolf Recapping

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:44.071
This episode is all about bridging the gap
between the old team and the new team, so

00:01:44.071 --> 00:01:48.680
naturally the car ride is used to tell the
story of Seasons 1 through 3.

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:52.780
Even the pre-history on how Paul became the
Alpha.

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:58.223
Kate is one of the craziest villains the show
has had and she's supposed to be a big part

00:01:58.223 --> 00:02:00.240
of the plot in Season 4.

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:03.679
She's not necessarily going to be the main
villain and I don't think she's the mysterious

00:02:03.679 --> 00:02:05.689
Benefactor that we've been teased with in
the trailers.

00:02:05.689 --> 00:02:07.710
But I'll talk about that in a sec.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:10.000
All this recapping is just setting us up for
next week when everyone comes to the realization

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.330
that you can't come back from the horrible
things that have happened.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:15.140
They can't just go back to being normal, they
have to push forward with what they have.

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:20.140
It's a metaphor for what happened with Derek,
the physical transformation and the show itself,

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:24.190
both Crystal Reed and Daniel Sharman asked
to leave the show and anytime a show loses

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:27.070
two major characters things get weird.

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:31.810
I don't think Teen Wolf is reinventing itself
in Season 4, but it is doing a soft reset,

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:34.380
which is why I think it's going to feel a
lot like Season 1 did.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.500
Which I will explain after my review.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.170
Number 3 - Lydia's Abilities Get Tested

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:40.770
Apparently killing people in whichever town
they're in is no big deal.

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:45.070
I love that nobody made a sound, no screams,
no police sirens.

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:48.930
This big test informs what's going to be happening
with Lydia's character this season.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:52.950
She's going to be developing her powers to
the point where she can be way more CSI with

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:54.340
the way she derives clues.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.460
Even though she and Stiles are reconnecting
I don't think there will be any real romance

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:57.820
between them, not a full on love triangle
with Malia, but I think she's going to use

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:59.120
Stiles as an anchor to reality.

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:03.230
She's probably grown more as a character since
Season 1 than anyone else on the show.

00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:07.980
I love Holland Roden, but Season 1 Lydia was
pretty off-putting before her transformation.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:09.730
That's just her hero's journey.

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:11.920
If you're not familiar with Joseph Campbell's
Hero with a Thousand Faces, it spells out

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:16.670
the archetypal Hero's journey from normal
person to hero.

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:20.320
A lot of fiction and television writers use
it to develop characters.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:24.530
Lydia's Journey in Season 4 is going to be
learning to master the supernatural and retain

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:25.530
her humanity.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:26.530
Becoming Master of both worlds.

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:28.090
The same thing is happening with the other
characters and their own situations like Scott

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:31.340
being the Alpha and Malia learning to be Human.

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:34.280
Number 2 - Derek Is Transformed into Young
Derek

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:39.060
The Derek we see is his younger self played
by the actor Ian Nelson who has played young

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:40.480
Derek in flashbacks.

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:45.280
There are a number of giant questions raised
by this including, what is the effect of the

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:50.810
Dark Moon on the Supernatural, what is the
significance of the Aztec Temple belonging

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:55.080
to the werejaguars and why was Derek intombed
behind a symbol of their god?

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:56.760
Who was the figure in Bone armor?

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:58.150
Because it definitely wasn't Kate.

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:00.560
She was busy harassing the Jeep crew while
Scott and Braeden were in the tombs.

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:04.220
And how is this all connected to the Benefactor
and the Deadpool List?

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:08.600
Since this episode was all about finding Derek,
presumably episode 2 will introduce the rest

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:12.340
of the new characters, the Benefactor and
the Deadpool.

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:16.770
The deadpool is both an awesome homage to
the comic book character Deadpool and it's

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:20.489
a kill list of all the supernatural creatures
living in Beacon Hills.

00:04:20.489 --> 00:04:24.449
It's like Teen Wolf is going to be paying
homage to Death Note this season and the Benefactor

00:04:24.449 --> 00:04:26.819
will be like the Light Yagami of the story.

00:04:26.819 --> 00:04:29.150
So if you liked that anime, you're going to
love season 4.

00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:32.430
and my Number 1 moment - WTF is Kate

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:34.860
It's pretty clear she's not just a werewolf.

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:39.259
Based on her taking Derek to the Aztec temple
I think we can assume she's a were jaguar.

00:04:39.259 --> 00:04:43.630
I love the way the show deepens the mythology
every season, last year got a little crazy

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:48.259
with the Kitsune, the Oni, Nemeton etcetera.

00:04:48.259 --> 00:04:52.389
Supposedly this season is supposed to be a
bit of a reprieve from the super dark direction

00:04:52.389 --> 00:04:53.389
things went.

00:04:53.389 --> 00:04:56.810
They're not just going to keep making it more
depressing and make us all feel awful every

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:57.810
week.

00:04:57.810 --> 00:05:00.909
That's why they're weaving a lot of familiar
things like Lacrosse back into the story in

00:05:00.909 --> 00:05:01.909
a big way.

00:05:01.909 --> 00:05:04.729
They're headed back to Beacon Hills, so I
think that the Benefactor will be someone

00:05:04.729 --> 00:05:07.550
using Kate to cause more chaos.

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:12.111
She's supposed to be a big part of the season,
but I'm pretty sure she's not the creature

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:14.169
with the bone armor Scott was fighting.

00:05:14.169 --> 00:05:17.980
That person was featured in the trailer, so
it's probably going to follow them back home

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:20.100
and cause a bunch of trouble between Lacrosse
Games.

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:24.150
I wouldn't be surprised if one of the new
characters turned out to be part of a were-jaguar

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:26.430
family that just moved to town and Kate was
working for them.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:29.250
But now it's your turn, let me know what your
favorite moment was.

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:31.550
And do you have a favorite ship already.

00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:35.490
They did say there wouldn't be a ton of romance,
but we'll definitely get some funny 'ship

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:36.490
moments.

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:41.069
I'm actually most excited to see Scott develop
his pack, an Alpha needs a pack.

00:05:41.069 --> 00:05:44.730
And there were a few spoilers about who would
be joining him but I don't want to say who

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:46.639
in this video just in case you don't want
to know.

00:05:46.639 --> 00:05:50.289
If you have heard the spoilers and what to
comment about it, just use the spoiler tags

00:05:50.289 --> 00:05:51.289
in the comments.

00:05:51.289 --> 00:05:54.363
Overall I gave the episode a B plus, next
to Legend of Korra it's going to be one of

00:05:54.363 --> 00:05:56.950
my favorite summer shows.

00:05:56.950 --> 00:06:01.009
It actually shares a lot in common with the
Avatar series.

00:06:01.009 --> 00:06:06.350
If you've never seen Last Airbender or Legend
of Korra, it revolves around this idea of

00:06:06.350 --> 00:06:09.319
the four elements, Air, Water, Earth and Fire.

00:06:09.319 --> 00:06:13.009
So each new season of Avatar is themed after
an element.

00:06:13.009 --> 00:06:16.620
The opening title scene of Teen Wolf also
revolves around elements, like when we had

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:21.979
the Red when Scott was becoming an Alpha which
represents the Air Element, during Season

00:06:21.979 --> 00:06:23.889
2 we had all the Water during the opening
titles.

00:06:23.889 --> 00:06:28.710
It's just a fun observation, but maybe the
Teen Wolf people are Avatar fans.

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:34.949
This season all that Sand makes me think season
4 will be earth element based.

00:06:34.949 --> 00:06:39.099
Usually the title scenes inform what the season
is going to be about.

00:06:39.099 --> 00:06:43.550
So be sure to write your theories for this
year in the comments.

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:44.910
The other thing that really stood out aside
from them trying really hard to balance between

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:50.499
what the show was last year and what it's
going to be this year is all of the characters

00:06:50.499 --> 00:06:55.120
relationships with each of the other characters.

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:59.870
The writers said this year is going to focus
much more on the human relationships as opposed

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:02.930
to the crazy supernatural relationships of
season 3.

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:05.300
That's why were going back to a ton of Lacrosse.

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:09.190
It's where we started in season 1 before Scott
and everyone got thrown into the supernatural

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:10.190
world.

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:14.740
The difference this time around is that everyone
is so much more mature, and because of all

00:07:14.740 --> 00:07:19.539
the new freshman characters, Scott, Stiles
and Lydia will be like mentors to them.

00:07:19.539 --> 00:07:23.250
Way better mentors than Derek was to Tyler
and Stiles.

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:24.330
Worst mentor ever.

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:25.770
Unless you count Paul.

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:28.970
So like I said, I'm going to be doing weekly
videos for Teen Wolf this season, be sure

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:29.970
to subscribe to get everything.

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:33.610
Be sure to let me know if you want me to do
bonus mythology videos and I'll start posting

00:07:33.610 --> 00:07:35.250
those Monday Mornings.

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:42.099
Right now click on either one of these annotations
to learn about Avatar Legend of Korra, it's

00:07:42.099 --> 00:07:45.129
starting this Friday and like I said it has
a lot in common with Teen Wolf thematically.

00:07:45.129 --> 00:07:47.960
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:48.759
High Fives!

